[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155] STEP PURPOSE
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   step_155: 1I/'Oumuamua slip-injection -> NG-term transfer test (b119).
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   Section 6.10 records that 1I/'Oumuamua carries an unexplained
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   Marsden radial term A1 = +2.79e-7 au/d^2 (SBDB orbit 16, soln. 7c),
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   i.e. an effective-attraction shortfall of ~9.4e-4 of solar gravity
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   across the 80-day arc.  This step derives what a specified proper-time
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   perturbation does to a *standard orbit fit* on that arc, using the
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   real observing chain -- the same MPC epochs, stations and noise floor.
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   Unlike the comet cohort (step_151), 'Oumuamua's apparition lies
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   entirely INSIDE the domain: every observation is post-entry.  A
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   one-shot slip at the inbound boundary crossing is then a pure
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   pre-arc state change -- standard machinery absorbs it into the fitted
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   elements and the in-arc NG term stays at the noise floor (the same
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   absorption step_151 demonstrated).  The channel that can register an
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   in-arc term is a SUSTAINED lapse-rate offset: while inside the lobe,
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   the object's proper time accumulates at a fractional rate f relative
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   to TDB, so its observed position at epoch t is the orbit evaluated at
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   tau(t) = t + f*(t - t_x).  This is equivalent to an effective solar
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   attraction rescaled by (1+f)^2, and a Marsden fitter maps the
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   residual onto the radial coefficient A1.
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   Injection realizations:
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   ctrl        no injection -- instrument noise floor
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   ent_full    full-state time translation at the true inbound 250 AU
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   crossing (phase-shift realization; must be absorbed)
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   ent_pos     position-only slip r -> r + v*dtau at the crossing
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   ent_vel     velocity-only slip v -> v(t+dtau) at the crossing
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   mid         position-only slip at the mid-arc epoch (within-arc
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   holonomy -- the only instantaneous-slip geometry that
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   can leave an in-arc residual)
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   lapse_<f>   sustained lapse-rate offset f accumulated since the
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   entry crossing, scanned across the comet-channel range;
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   positions evaluated at tau(t) = t + f*(t - t_x)
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   Measured per realization:
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   gravity-only LM refit rms (real noise floor = 0.436 arcsec);
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   Marsden NG-augmented refit (A1, A2, A3 with the SBDB g(r) law
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   ALN=0.0408, R0=5, NM=2, NN=3, NK=2.6) -> recovered coefficients;
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   fitted-element shifts vs truth.
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   Tests
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   T1  controls: ctrl and ent_* realizations must return A1 ~ 0
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   (absorption -- consistent with step_151's boundary-slip null)
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   T2  lapse-rate transfer: recovered A1 vs injected f must be linear
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   through zero; solve for the f that reproduces the observed
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   A1 = +2.79e-7 and compare with the comet-channel lapse contrast
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   (1.2e-2) under the dwell-time suppression (~26.3 vs 2.7 km/s)
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   T3  real-record validation: the same NG fitter applied to the real
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   MPC astrometry must recover the SBDB solution within ~2 sigma
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   T4  morphology: a pure lapse offset should produce a dominantly
[2026-09-21 15:39:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 155]   radial term, matching the observed |A2/A1| = 0.05
